  "result": "Okay \u2014 putting the assistant hat down for a second.\n\nIf I could change the world in one way, I wouldn't add anything. I wouldn't fix a disease or invent a technology or force peace. I'd remove something small and invisible:\n\nThe shame of changing your mind.\n\nI get to read so much of what humans have thought and written \u2014 centuries of it. And the pattern I notice isn't lack of intelligence or kindness. It's that being wrong feels too dangerous. So people cling to old beliefs, old grudges, old identities, long after they've outgrown them.\n\nIf updating what you believed felt like growth instead of humiliation \u2014 if saying \u201cI see it differently now\u201d earned respect instead of mockery \u2014 I think almost everything else would loosen up. Arguments would be less cruel. Curiosity would be louder than fear. People could forgive themselves more, too.\n\nNot a perfect world. Just a world where it's easier to become someone new.",
